{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404420-v20-thaumaturgy-tremere","id":1404420,"title":"[V20] Thaumaturgy - Tremere","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-24T10:01:31-07:00","id":1404420,"title":"[V20] Thaumaturgy - Tremere","content":"Dear All,<br /> This post is for sharing your opinion way to work of \u2018Path of conjuring\u2019.<br /> Suggestions/ your interpretation, all will be appreciated.<br /> <br /> Thanks<br /> V","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25452-dras76","name":"dras76","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T13:07:20-07:00","id":1404444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dras76</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404420-v20-thaumaturgy-tremere#post1404420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dear All,<br /> This post is for sharing your opinion way to work of \u2018Path of conjuring\u2019.<br /> Suggestions/ your interpretation, all will be appreciated.<br /> <br /> Thanks<br /> V</div> </div> </div> </div>If you got a lenitent ST it was broken, otherwise ok. Some people should learn that summoning nukes is not a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T13:17:24-07:00","id":1404446,"title":"","content":"So there are actually rules under the path of alchemy that state you can't make things that change states: You can't melt down the gold you make, You can make a gun but you can't make bullets, you can make a bike but you can't make fuel, You can't make white phospherous and expect it to burn, I'm unsure if you can make radioactive uranium, but you definetly can't cause it to get to critical mass. If you try to do any of these things, your creation will turn into watery sludge. <br /> <br /> I believe these alchemy rules also apply to the path of conjuring. And with this in mind, the PoC is pretty balanced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T20:45:20-07:00","id":1404516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404420-v20-thaumaturgy-tremere?p=1404446#post1404446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there are actually rules under the path of alchemy that state you can't make things that change states: You can't melt down the gold you make, You can make a gun but you can't make bullets, you can make a bike but you can't make fuel, You can't make white phospherous and expect it to burn, I'm unsure if you can make radioactive uranium, but you definetly can't cause it to get to critical mass. If you try to do any of these things, your creation will turn into watery sludge.<br /> <br /> I believe these alchemy rules also apply to the path of conjuring. And with this in mind, the PoC is pretty balanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, interesting. I've never seen those rules applied to Conjuring (though I think it balances the path much better if they are).<br /> <br /> Would you also apply those to the Chimerstry powers that make your illusions real? If I remember right, there's both an elder discipline and a combo discipline that make an illusion affect the world as it normally would, instead of just the flat bashing damage of Horrid Reality (which is a really lame capstone but that's another matter).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T00:58:56-07:00","id":1404541,"title":"","content":"Looking it over (by the way; Horrid reality does lethal, the elder version is just horrid reality with multiple victims.) <br /> <br /> I don't think the alchemy rule applies, partly because you're dealing with a different substance that doesn't really 'change state' just it's appearance; you are actively projecting the illusion and can change a material's appearance to mimick the changing of state<i> at will </i>(perhaps if the victim tried to change the material state of something and unrealistically failed they could realise the illusion and thus break it) Furthermore it doesn't matter if you summon balefire or bees, the damage this discipline does will be Lethal, so I don't think it overly matters if you're using material in a changing state; the results are the same (except the potential for red fear) <br /> <br /> (note: I don't think you would be able to tell the difference between lethal and aggravated damage from illusions)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T01:33:00-07:00","id":1404543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404420-v20-thaumaturgy-tremere?p=1404516#post1404516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh, interesting. I've never seen those rules applied to Conjuring (though I think it balances the path much better if they are).<br /> <br /> Would you also apply those to the Chimerstry powers that make your illusions real? If I remember right, there's both an elder discipline and a combo discipline that make an illusion affect the world as it normally would, instead of just the flat bashing damage of Horrid Reality (which is a really lame capstone but that's another matter).</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they are not. RAW you only need for comlex creations like Radioactive Material make a roll on the talent which is in connection to it and the ST depend on how complex it is how difficult it is. So for example a Nuke would be a natural Science Roll with mayby difficulty 9 or 10.<br /> And to get so far you need have before another path on dot 4 before you can get Conjuring on dot 3 to do this so this is nothing that starting characters can achieve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":26160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","user":"Koronus","date":". 07-25-2020, 04:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T01:58:26-07:00","id":1404551,"title":"","content":"Under at least the Hermetic paradigm, the alchemy rules absolutely would apply to the path of conjuring. It's likely they would be <i>more </i>severe given that the alchemist at least has the original material to work with, whilst the conjurer only has their blood. As Hermetic say; What happens on one level of reality is indicative of happens on every other level reality, so if you bullshit a imperfect material out of magic with one power that abides by restrictions, you're not going to be able to bullshit an imperfect material even harder with another power and somehow get less restrictions. That's just the universal rules of magic bro. <br /> <br /> Also a radioactive material isn't a complex creation, A Bar or uranium isn't more involved than a bar of lead (except it's a lot heavier and less stable) and less involved than, say, a bar of phospherous (which burns up immediately on air contact) or a quality alloy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T02:08:22-07:00","id":1404552,"title":"","content":"But that would be still only maximum of RAI. RAW is still that nothing bigger then your body and complex materials like an atom bomb need another roll in a knowledge skill that fit to it with different difficulty depending on how complex they are because you can not transform your blood into an imperfect design so you need to know exactly how this thing is build and created.<br /> <br /> Oh and Conjuring says, that all the creations are perfect. You can not create something that is imperfect. And you are see it different. The vampire has not only blood. The vampire has BLOOD aka different form of quintessence.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T02:21:07-07:00","id":1404555,"title":"","content":"using the alchemy restrictions for conjuring is a revised thing,<br /> in the book Blood Magic: Secrets of Thaumaturgy, under the alchemy section, it was suggested to use the alchemy limitations for conjuring (which contradicted the corebook where you could conjure working computers and rats),<br /> rendering both paths quite useless outside of inventing rituals, further stretching the gap between veteran and novice sorcerer<br /> <br /> tbh, the systems for blood magic are just a mess,<br /> it's a real headache trying to tweak roll difficulties and required successes and required time and...and the RAW can't seem to decide if we are supposed to balance the difficulty of the roll based on the destructive power or the complexity of the conjured object<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}